// A HELD RESUME THROUGH A `!Alloc` CALLEE — the remainder runs in its extent.
// `plus_one` declares `!Alloc` and calls its callback; the callback resumes a
// held continuation (plus_one computes after it returns, so the op is
// multi-shot and `resume` calls the record), so the remainder runs inside
// plus_one's extent, and its row carries the op's own cost. The resume
// performs its continuation's world — the handler's remainder cell — so the
// callback's row carries it into plus_one's gate, and the install judges the
// gate against its own remainder: E_EffectMismatch naming plus_one. Every
// boot through 477bb667 compiled it and ran it to 21, the gate seeing a Pure
// callback (Hβ.continuations.spine-callee-row-is-blind-to-the-held-resume).
effect Cell {
  bump() -> Int
}

fn plus_one(f) with !Alloc = f() + 1

handler cell with s = 10 {
  bump() => plus_one(() => resume(s)),
}

fn body() = bump() * 2

fn main() = {
  body()
} ~> cell
